@flexiarg writing-coherence/and-yet-as-problem-frame
@title State the Contrast With 'And Yet', Then Frame It as the Problem
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-BvxmAN turn-FGKYBD
@parent futon-theory/structural-tension-as-observation
@context Rewriting the substitution paragraph for the staging-site document.

! conclusion: Join the two in one sentence with an explicit contrastive pivot ('and yet…') and adopt the unresolved contrast as the problem statement.

  + IF:
    A capability (LLMs trained on nearly all published knowledge) coexists with a failure (the knowledge economy remains inaccessible).

  + HOWEVER:
    Stating the capability alone flatters the technology; stating the failure alone reads as complaint.

  + THEN:
    Join the two in one sentence with an explicit contrastive pivot ('and yet…') and adopt the unresolved contrast as the problem statement.

  + BECAUSE:
    Structural tension is treated as the observation; here the contrast sentence makes the tension visible and the framing instruction adopts it as the problem the document will work on.
